9. If a match is found, increment the word count.
10. Discard any remaining characters in the stringstream until the next delimiter.
11. Close the input file.
12. Output the count of the search word occurrences.

Note that this implementation assumes the search word is a single word without any spaces or special characters. If the search word can have these variations, you'll need to modify the code accordingly, for example, by using a regular expression to match the search word, or by comparing the lowercased/cased versions of the word against all the words in each line.

