f(x) &= 5x^3 - 2x + 3 \\
f(2) &= 5(2^3) - 2(2) + 3 \quad \text{(Substituting 2 for x)} \\
&= 5(8) - 2(2) + 3 \\
&= 40 - 4 + 3 \\
&= \boxed{\text{39}} \quad \text{(The value of f(2))}
\end{align} 

Therefore, when $x=2$, the value of the function $f(x) = 5x^3 - 2x + 3$ is $39$.
